IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc15-duties`

-- ccc15-tests-duties.l4 -- the regulative rules of ccc15-duties.l4 run with #TRACE. A DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT on the stable binary,
-- so the traces carry no assertion: the expected outcome is written beside each trace from the text (and from the HENCE/LEST polarity of MUST, MAY and SHANT) before the run,
-- the run is read with both stable builds by hand (NOTES.md records both outcomes), and the same duties are ASSERTED as decision functions in the tests of the twin modules.
-- What can be asserted (measured on 1.6.110 and 1.6.109, NOTES.md): a rule whose gate is unmet is the value FULFILLED, and `EQUALS FULFILLED` on it is satisfied; a rule whose gate is met is a standing
-- obligation or permission, and comparing it is "could not be evaluated" (counted as failed by check.sh), so that side is exercised by #TRACE only. The assertions at the end are the unmet-gate ones.

§ `Traces`

-- Every MAY: exercised, FULFILLED; the gate unmet, nothing is permitted and nothing is owed, FULFILLED. (A permission unused lapses with no consequence, which the text states none for.)
-- 473(1.1): a judge MAY order that any offence be tried in conjunction.
#TRACE `s 473(1.1) the judge's permission to order that any offence be tried in conjunction with the listed offence` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 473(1.1) order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469` AT 1
#TRACE `s 473(1.1) the judge's permission to order that any offence be tried in conjunction with the listed offence` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 473(1.1) order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469` AT 1
-- 474(1) and (2): the clerk MAY adjourn.
#TRACE `s 474(1) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn when no jury panel is to be summoned` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the clerk of the court` DOES `s 474(1) adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` AT 1
#TRACE `s 474(1) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn when no jury panel is to be summoned` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the clerk of the court` DOES `s 474(1) adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` AT 1
#TRACE `s 474(2) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn on the instructions of a judge` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the clerk of the court` DOES `s 474(2) adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` AT 1
#TRACE `s 474(2) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn on the instructions of a judge` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the clerk of the court` DOES `s 474(2) adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` AT 1
-- 475(1)(b), the proviso and (2): the court MAY continue, adjourn, continue after adjourning, and draw an inference.
#TRACE `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court's permission to continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 475(1)(b)(i) continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` AT 2
#TRACE `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court's permission to continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 475(1)(b)(i) continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` AT 2
#TRACE `s 475(1)(b)(ii) the court's permission to adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 475(1)(b)(ii) adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` AT 2
#TRACE `s 475(1) the court's permission to continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 475(1) continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` AT 5
#TRACE `s 475(2) the court's permission to draw an adverse inference` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 475(2) draw an inference adverse to the accused from the fact that the accused has absconded` AT 5
-- 482.1(3): a court, justice or judge MAY issue a summons or warrant. A justice, and a judge, are parties too.
#TRACE `s 482.1(3) the permission of a court, justice or judge to issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused` `a justice` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 482.1(3) issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings` AT 1
#TRACE `s 482.1(3) the permission of a court, justice or judge to issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused` `a judge` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 482.1(3) issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings` AT 1

-- 478(1): the court SHANT try an offence committed entirely in another province. Gate met (the decision function says JUST TRUE) and the court tries it: BREACH BY the court.
#TRACE `s 478(1) the prohibition on a court in a province from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 478(1) try an offence committed entirely in another province` AT 3
-- the court does not try it: the prohibition stands and is respected (no period is stated, so the trace prints the standing prohibition back)
#TRACE `s 478(1) the prohibition on a court in a province from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
-- gate unmet (JUST FALSE: an exception displaces the bar) or not covered (NOTHING): no prohibition is derived: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 478(1) the prohibition on a court in a province from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 478(1) try an offence committed entirely in another province` AT 3
#TRACE `s 478(1) the prohibition on a court in a province from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 478(1) try an offence committed entirely in another province` AT 3

-- 478(3) and 479: the court MUST determine the accused who consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty to be guilty. Done: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 478(3) the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 478(3) determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` AT 3
-- the accused does not plead guilty: no duty arises: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 478(3) the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 478(3) determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` AT 3
-- the duty states no period, so with no event the duty stands and the trace prints it back (the same trace waited on does not breach)
#TRACE `s 478(3) the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)
#TRACE `s 479 the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 479 determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` AT 3
#TRACE `s 479 the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- 482.1(2): the parties shall comply with a direction made in accordance with a case management rule. The accused complies: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 482.1(2) the party's duty to comply with the direction` `the accused` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 482.1(2) comply with the direction` AT 4
-- the prosecutor is a party too
#TRACE `s 482.1(2) the party's duty to comply with the direction` `the prosecutor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 482.1(2) comply with the direction` AT 4
-- not a direction made in accordance with a rule under (1): no duty arises under the subsection: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 482.1(2) the party's duty to comply with the direction` `the accused` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 482.1(2) comply with the direction` AT 4
-- no period is stated, so the unperformed duty stands: the residual obligation is printed
#TRACE `s 482.1(2) the party's duty to comply with the direction` `the accused` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

§ `Assertions: where the gate is unmet no duty, permission or prohibition arises (the value is FULFILLED)`

#ASSERT `s 473(1.1) the judge's permission to order that any offence be tried in conjunction with the listed offence` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 474(1) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn when no jury panel is to be summoned` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 474(1) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn when no jury panel is to be summoned` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 474(2) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn on the instructions of a judge` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court's permission to continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(ii) the court's permission to adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(ii) the court's permission to adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 475(1) the court's permission to continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 475(1) the court's permission to continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 475(2) the court's permission to draw an adverse inference` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 478(1) the prohibition on a court in a province from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 478(1) the prohibition on a court in a province from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` NOTHING EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 478(3) the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 479 the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 482.1(2) the party's duty to comply with the direction` `the accused` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT `s 482.1(3) the permission of a court, justice or judge to issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused` `a judge` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
